     throw new Error('Cannot assign reference to prototype')
   }
   ```
   This intercepts the malicious segment before any prototype-bound operations occur, throwing a visible error and stopping the pollution. Developers can verify the fix by running this PoC: it should fail with the specific error message in patched versions, while successfully polluting the prototype in vulnerable ones.

