- Run this in a controlled environment with CPU monitoring (e.g., `top` or `perf`). You will observe a sharp CPU spike and measurable time increase on the vulnerable regex execution.
- The patch shown in your commit correctly neutralizes the issue by using `[^*]|\*(?!\/)` to prevent overlapping matches inside comment blocks, making the backtrack tree strictly linear (`O(n)`) instead of exponential (`O(2^n)`).
- For production, ensure all CodeMirror instances use the patched version or sanitize/heuristic-limit input sizes when syntax highlighting untrusted code.

