2. **Exponential Backtracking in V8**: When the regex engine scans a long string composed entirely of spaces, at every position it must decide which branch to take: match `\s+` anchored to the start, or match `\s+` anchored to the end. Because both can successfully consume overlapping sequences of whitespace, the engine cannot short-circuit and instead explores **all possible combination paths**.
3. **O(2ⁿ) Complexity**: This ambiguity causes exponential time complexity. A string of just 500 spaces can trigger millions of backtrack states. Scaling to `repeat(5000)` guarantees the engine will exhaustively try every permutation until it hits V8's configured maximum backtracking depth (30,000), resulting in a `RangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded` or a complete CPU hang depending on execution mode.
